// Pull request author: damnkrishna
// Change: new rule
// Title: MFA Bypass Via Windows Hello PIN Or Credential Provider Registry Tampering
// Sigma ID: f514d72b-9c1c-4109-bc9f-1674486af72f
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Krishna Gupta
// Date: 2026-08-08 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-evasion, T1556.006
// Description: Detects registry modifications that disable domain PIN sign-in (AllowDomainPINLogon) or disable
//   a Credential Provider, both of which can be used to weaken or bypass multi-factor authentication
//   enforcement on a Windows host.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators deliberately disabling convenience PIN sign-in or a specific credential provider as part of a hardening baseline
// References:
//   - https://gpedit.tplant.com.au/en-us/policy/CredentialProviders/AllowDomainPINLogon/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-credentialproviders
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f2aeee5b997d7767b5c833ad128cb3c04e29095d/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_mfa_credential_provider_tampering.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey endswith "\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\AllowDomainPINLogon" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)") or (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Authentication\\Credential Providers.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\Disabled" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)")
